GradleMaven <pre><code>implementation 'io.github.seonwkim:actor-spring-boot-starter:1.0.0'
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
  &lt;groupId&gt;io.github.seonwkim&lt;/groupId&gt;
  &lt;artifactId&gt;actor-spring-boot-starter&lt;/artifactId&gt;
  &lt;version&gt;1.0.0&lt;/version&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre> <p>The latest version is on Maven Central. For cluster features (sharding, singletons, replicated data), use <code>actor-spring-boot-starter-cluster</code> instead. Other modules are listed on the home page.</p> <p>Writing Kotlin? Add <code>io.github.seonwkim:actor-kotlin:1.0.0</code> too, for <code>suspend</code> functions and reified helpers (see the Kotlin guide). Every code sample in these docs has a Java and a Kotlin tab; your choice applies to the whole site.</p>

0.x 1.0 <code>spring-boot-starter-actor</code>, <code>spring-boot-starter-actor_3</code> <code>actor-spring-boot-starter</code> <code>spring-boot-starter-actor-metrics</code> <code>actor-metrics</code> (cluster features were in the one artifact) <code>actor-spring-boot-starter-cluster</code> <p>The old coordinates publish relocation POMs for 1.0.0, so a build that still names them resolves to the new artifacts and prints a relocation warning. Switch to the new names; the relocations are not kept after this release.</p> GradleMaven <pre><code>implementation 'io.github.seonwkim:actor-spring-boot-starter:1.0.0'
// cluster applications use this instead:
// implementation 'io.github.seonwkim:actor-spring-boot-starter-cluster:1.0.0'
</code></pre> <pre><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
